id: pm-vitestredirect
title: Vitest redirect allowlist misses Windows backslash traversal
description: "Public interceptor redirect registration checks a POSIX-joined pathname before Windows interprets backslashes at file read. Requires a reachable public handler and Windows filesystem semantics. Tracked Node suites do not establish application exploitability. Upstream: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xp26-3454-mjgp. The locked development dependency is affected; version4.1.12 is patched."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: dependencies,security,vitest
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:12:38.826Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T21:20:53.662Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T21:20:50.939Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T21:20:50.939Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "Inspect the upstream shared boundary and alternate representations; Preserve legitimate test and benchmark behavior; Verify exact lock, fresh advisories and native Windows CI before merge"
parent: pm-vitest4112
risk: medium
confidence: 95
severity: medium
resolution: "Upgrade Vitest and coverage-v8 together to4.1.12, remove affected locked mocker4.1.11, add real installed-handler regression controls and version the existing scanner recurrence family. Preserve CodSpeed5.7.1, Vite7 and normal release-age/cooldown policy."
expected_result: Both advisory boundaries are repaired in the locked development toolchain and legitimate test/benchmark behavior remains intact under strict full-lock advisory admission.
actual_result: Both regressions fail against4.1.11 and pass against4.1.12. The linked focused cohort passes9/9; frozen install/build/typechecks and dedicated benchmarks pass. Fresh registry+OSV cover all568 locked versions with zero positives. Independent candidate review found no concrete bypass or regression. Native Windows CI and whole-project coverage remain required before merge; no CLI/SDK exploit or publication is claimed.
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:12:38.826Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus3042/3042 including closed items has no occurrence of either advisory or predecessor GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9. Live request-specific searches and open/in_progress inventories found no exact advisory owner; semantic-only search results are not duplicate evidence. Reuse the security epic; keep the broader Vitest5 migration separately open."
  "2026-10-21T21:17:00.518Z","harness:codex","Boundary and compatibility evidence: both public plugin regressions fail against4.1.11 and pass against4.1.12. The generated-source test executes only a harmless synthetic sentinel in a disposable Node child and also verifies exact URL preservation, quotes/backslashes/newlines in export names and asynchronous binding updates. The redirect test exercises the real registration handler and Vite allowlist without reading any files, rejects slash/backslash and nested escapes, and preserves an allowed redirect. This tests the normalization-to-allowlist boundary portably; native Windows CI remains required before merge. No tracked application config registers these public handlers, so no CLI/SDK exploit is claimed."
  "2026-10-21T21:17:01.616Z","harness:codex","Fresh patched evidence at21:13UTC: both feeds complete over all568 locked versions with zero positives; the previous hosted569-version receipt remains the positive before-control. Frozen installation, build and all typecheck targets pass. Existing retry/reporter/CodSpeed runtime cohort passes7/7, new handler regressions pass2/2, and the dedicated benchmark invocation succeeds. Paired4.1.12 packages satisfy pnpm default one-day age without exclusions; Vitest5 and CodSpeed6 migration remains separate."
  "2026-10-21T21:20:49.926Z","harness:codex",Independent candidate review found no concrete surviving bypass or regression. It traced all three shared serialization sites and redirect normalization before allowlist admission and the unchanged checked-path read. Additional read-only controls covered nine redirect representations and five export-name classes. Linux boundary execution passed; native Windows acceptance and whole-project coverage remain required hosted gates before merge.
